    "explanation": "This is a route-deviation case, and both parties should read the ruling against the same record. Under POL-RD-22 the deviation is the platform's recorded distances: 9.5 km actual less 8.1 km recommended = 1.40 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance, so a refund is due and the within-tolerance rows (c) and (e) of POL-RD-24 do not apply.\n\nNotification (POL-RD-21). The chat log carries two messages only, sent 08:35:52 and 08:36:12, both before the trip began at 08:37:22 and both about the pickup point ('I'm at Westgate taxi stand, white Corolla' / 'Ok'); messages_during_trip is empty and there is no call recording. The driver's own filed statement concedes 'Forgot to inform, sorry.' The rider's 'Ok' answered a pickup message and cannot be an acknowledgment of a deviation that the record places at 08:42:55, minutes later. Row (a) of POL-RD-24 — no refund where the rider agreed — is therefore unavailable.\n\nTraffic justification (POL-RD-23). The LTA advisory is a HEAVY_TRAFFIC advisory, an admissible congestion type, on the Pan-Island Expressway towards Changi, covering 'after Clementi Avenue 6 exit to Clementi Road exit', valid 08:15:42 to 09:27:22 and so overlapping the trip window (08:37:22 to 08:55:22). That stretch lies on the recommended route, which the trip record gives as PIE ... Clementi Road ... Holland Road, and it is exactly where the trace and the event log place the vehicle leaving the recommended route at 08:42:55. The advisory therefore intersects the recommended route and justifies the reroute: this is row (b) — traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation over 1 km. The refund is the same under row (d) if the justification were rejected, so the outcome does not turn on it.\n\nAmount (POL-RD-24). The excess distance fare is deviation 1.40 km × per-km rate 0.72 SGD = 1.008, rounded to 1.01 SGD, without surge — the figure the fare ledger's own derived money block records. The rider asked for 4.00 SGD, but the matrix moves only the excess distance fare, so the refund is 1.01 SGD, not 4.00. The single ERP toll of 1.00 SGD was incurred at 08:40:36 on the recommended stretch, before the deviation, and is not added. The ledger shows 14.78 SGD charged and 0.00 refunded, so 1.01 SGD still moves to the rider.\n\nForum and confidence. The contested value of 4.00 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence, and no fraud flag appears on either profile, so no 0.95 uplift applies; POL-RD-25's 0.80 bar for a route deviation is met. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact — trip record, GPS trace, chat log, fare ledger and advisory — is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so POL-GEN-02's impairment cap bites on nothing and POL-GEN-26 leaves no open question to escalate. Both profile histories are context only under POL-GEN-01 and decide nothing about this trip."
